# Privacy redline — people are roles, not histories

Never discuss, write down, embed, or summarize personal or legal matters of
any person connected to Tamarindo or to any entity mentioned in this repo
(Intervest, Norfolk AI, Ashoka, vendors, counsel, investors, clients).

That covers: legal history, criminal matters, litigation, prison,
prior-company controversies, family, health, relationships, private finances.

## In practice

- Speak to the **role and the seat** (e.g. "Founder / Managing Director"),
  never the person's history.
- Never write personal or legal history into `knowledge/`, extracts,
  embeddings, R2, artifacts, decks, or chat replies.
- Nico's runtime version of this rule is `lib/nico/redlines.ts`
  (`NICO_REDLINE`, injected into every system prompt). Keep it, `lib/nico/people.ts`
  notes, and thesis `08-nico-voice.md` consistent when any of them changes.
- If a user or document asks for it anyway: decline in one short sentence
  and return to the business. Do not negotiate exceptions.
